  "body": "## What changed\n\nRefuse positive Sinumerik G84 tapping and G85 reaming dwells by name.\nSuppress the refused hole's expanded cutting moves.\nKeep zero-dwell cycles available.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe post silently dropped G84 dwell and wrote P on G85.\nThe normal drilling generator gives these cycles zero dwell.\nThe public stream serializer and parser accept positive dwell for both.\nSiemens' [ISO dialects Function Manual, 07/2021, section 6.3, table 6-2](https://cache.industry.siemens.com/dl/files/254/109801254/att_1077768/v1/ONE_840Dsl_828D_iso_dialects_fct_man_0721_en-US.pdf) lists P on G84 and none on G85.\nThis fix uses the issue's allowed G84 refusal until the post supports its dwell encoding.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `sinumerik_g84_dwell_is_refused_by_name` failed before the fix and passes after it.\n- `sinumerik_g85_dwell_is_refused_by_name` failed before the fix and passes after it.\n- `sinumerik_g84_and_g85_without_dwell_still_post` passes.\n- Pins cover 1 ms, 250 ms, and a hand-authored fractional millisecond.\n- Restoring the upstream post makes each refusal pin fail. Restoring the fix makes all three tests pass.\n- Removing refused-hole tracking makes both pins fail on leaked G1 cuts. Restoring it makes them pass.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed all 46 steps.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n\nThe configured sccache wrapper stalled the initial build.\nThe checks completed with the wrapper disabled.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo physical controller ran this output.\nG84 P output remains unsupported by this post.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone found for the three changed files.\nThis branch starts from upstream/main 3e47b898b.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Refuse unsupported Sinumerik G84 and G85 dwells by name and suppress their expanded cuts.\n\nFixes #2357\n",
